  "query_preview": "../Thursday through Sunday/...\nOnshore flow with at times moderate showers continue for Thursday\nwith the stacked but weakening low lingering over the northern \nGulf. The low will shift southeast and weaken further Thursday \nnight into Friday, with showers diminishing from north to south \nacross the panhandle. Any lingering showers across the southern \npanhandle should by Friday afternoon. A few lingering snow showers\npossible for Thursday along the Klondike Highway and the upper \nreaches of the Haines Highway but any accumulations would be \nminimal. As the low departs to the southeast, ensemble and \ndeterministic guidance generally show upper-level ridge over \nmainland Alaska shifting east and settling over SEAK Friday into \nthe weekend, with clearing skies and drier offshore flow \ndeveloping. Gusty northerly winds could develop along the northern\nhighway into Lynn Canal. Daytime highs will remain in the 40s \nthroughout the period, with overnight lows in the 30s.",
